{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 54, :comments ["<b>And you shall take possession of the land by lot.</b> The commentators were greatly troubled by this verse, saying that the beginning of the parashah speaks of the destruction of the nations and their molten images, and so too the end of the parashah: ״וְאִם לֹא תוֹרִישׁוּ אֶת יוֹשְׁבֵי הָאָרֶץ״ and so forth — and how did the verse ״וְהִתְנַחַלְתֶּם אֶת הָאָרֶץ״ get inserted between these joined passages? And I say that it is not difficult at all, for in the destruction of the idols and the high places and the driving out of all the nations, HaShem imposed a great labor upon Israel, and there is cause to fear two things: first, that the matter would be like the pot of partners, and this commandment would fall away, for each person would say it is possible for the mitzvah of destruction to be fulfilled through others; second, that it would cause dissension among the tribes, for each one would choose the lesser evil for himself in a place where there are not many idols and molten images. Therefore He inserted into this subject the verse ״וְהִתְנַחַלְתֶּם אֶת הָאָרֶץ בְּגוֹרָל״, for by this all the concerns were nullified."], :book :numbers, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:44:00.431483724Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}